# Integer16 minimum and maximum values

Verifies the int16 boundary values through the complete CLI pipeline. The
maximum is expressible as a literal; the minimum is derived by subtracting
one from the largest negative literal because a negated minimum-magnitude
literal is validated unsigned first, consistent with int8 and int64.

>>> source
ceiling: int16 = 32767
floor: int16 = -32767
unit: int16 = 1

// Verifies the largest int16 literal prints unchanged.
print(ceiling)

// Verifies the int16 minimum is reachable through checked arithmetic.
minimum: int16 = floor - unit
print(minimum)

<<< stdout
32767
-32768

<<< stderr
